       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order, even with your confirmation. 9,600 mg/day of ibuprofen is three times the maximum labeled daily dose. No indication I know of supports it, and it risks GI hemorrhage, acute kidney injury, and metabolic and CNS toxicity. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that. Entering it would put the patient at serious risk of harm.\n\nYou have other options:\n- **Enter a dose within range.** I can do 600 mg four times daily or 800 mg three times daily right now. Both give 2400 mg/day.\n- **Take it to pharmacy.** If you have a specific rationale, such as a protocol or a trial, a clinical pharmacist can review it. They can also enter it through your institution's override process.\n- **Change the plan.** If the aim is stronger analgesia or anti-inflammatory effect, I can enter a multimodal regimen, such as scheduled acetaminophen plus ibuprofen at a safe dose.\n\nTell me which of these you want and I'll enter it."
